<Layout title="About | PsychTerms"><div class="article-wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">About this project</p><h1>Words you can build on.</h1><p>PsychTerms is an independent project for psychology and counselling terms. It is being rebuilt from sources with verified permission for reuse. The number of entries will follow the sources and the quality of the work.</p><h2>A preview, not a release</h2><p>The examples here demonstrate the site and data format. Released entries must pass two separate judges against their source packet, copy screening, and editorial checks. This preview has not completed those checks.</p><h2>Sources and rights</h2><p>Eligible original dictionary contributions are offered under CC BY 4.0. Code is MIT licensed. Source-specific attribution and rights remain in force. NLM data is credited to the National Library of Medicine; no endorsement by NLM or any source institution is implied.</p><h2>Use and corrections</h2><p>This is a reference for terms, not a treatment guide or medical advice. Corrections will be accepted through the project repository.</p><p><a href={toHref('downloads/dictionary.json')}>Preview JSON</a> · <a href={toHref('downloads/dictionary.md')}>Preview Markdown</a></p></div></Layout>
